      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s one‑room adobe schoolhouse, built in 1915, sits beside the historic depot on the east bank of the Babocomari River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://patagoniaregionaltimes.org/glimpses-from-our-past-the-babocomari-creek-bridge/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1922, contractors Frank Lown and Tom Woods constructed a steel bridge over the Babocomari River that locals still remember.",
